meta {
  name: Servers
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.get_servers
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("items have the SRV fields", function () {
    expect(res.body.message).to.be.an("array");
    res.body.message.forEach(function (s) {
      ["status", "status_checked_at", "site_url", "last_backup", "overdue", "erpnext_version", "region_label", "backup_policy_name", "backup_frequency", "backup_retention"].forEach(function (k) {
        expect(s).to.have.property(k);
      });
      expect(s.status).to.be.oneOf(["online", "degraded", "offline", null]);
    });
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Lists the client's hosted servers.

  **Endpoint:** `GET /api/method/implementor.client_api.get_servers`  
  **Screen:** Hosting list. Home and the Services list get the same items from `get_services` → `hosting[]`.

  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). Only records of the user's own client company are returned.

  **Query parameters:**

  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Not used by the app. The server picks the user's company. Disabled by default. |

  **Response:**

  ```json
  {
    "message": [
      {
        "name": "s6qivo97hn",
        "server_name": "hamza-erp-prod",
        "site_url": "erp.hamza.sa",
        "environment": "Production",
        "provider": "OCI",
        "region": "me-jeddah-1",
        "region_label": "Jeddah",
        "status": "online",
        "status_checked_at": "2026-11-06T09:30:00+03:00",
        "erpnext_version": "v15.40.0",
        "backup_schedule": "Daily 02:00 AST, 14-day retention + weekly offsite",
        "backup_frequency": "Daily, 02:00 AST",
        "backup_retention": "14 days + weekly offsite",
        "backup_policy_name": "OCI Gold",
        "last_backup": { "at": "2026-11-06T02:00:12+03:00", "state": "confirmed" },
        "overdue": false,
        "ssl_expiry": "2027-01-10",
        "ssl_days_left": 65,
        "last_restore_test": "2026-10-15"
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  **Fields:**

  - `name`: send this as `server` to Server Details and Backups.
  - `server_name`: internal name. Show `site_url` on the card instead, when set.
  - `site_url`: the client's site, e.g. `erp.hamza.sa`. Null if not entered yet.
  - `environment`: `Production`, `Staging` or `Dev`, as stored (not lowercased). Can be null.
  - `provider`, `region`: free text, e.g. `OCI`, `me-jeddah-1`. Can be null.
  - `region_label`: city name for `region`. Null for a region we haven't labelled; show `region` then.
  - `status`: lowercase code: `online`, `degraded` (answered with an HTTP error or took more than 3 seconds) or `offline` (no answer within 10 seconds). Null if never checked (for example no `site_url`); hide the chip then.
  - `status_checked_at`: when the status was last checked. Null if never checked.
  - `erpnext_version`: text. Can be null.
  - `backup_schedule`: free text written by our team. Can be null.
  - `backup_frequency`: when backups run, short text written by our team, e.g. "Daily, 02:00 AST". Null until filled in.
  - `backup_retention`: how long backups are kept, short text written by our team, e.g. "14 days + weekly offsite". Null until filled in.
  - `backup_policy_name`: the OCI policy name, e.g. "OCI Gold". Null when no OCI policy is known: OCI isn't configured, the server has no backup policy, or there is no successful OCI read in the last 24 hours.
  - `last_backup`: for "Last backup today 02:00 · Confirmed". Null when there's no data.
    - When a recent OCI read exists, this is the newest OCI run. It is null if OCI returned no runs, even when our team recorded a backup time.
    - Otherwise it is the time recorded by our team, with `state` `recorded`. Null if none was recorded.
    - `at`: date-time of the newest backup.
    - `state`: `confirmed`, `running`, `queued`, `failed`, `deleted`, or `recorded` (entered by our team, not read from OCI). Any other OCI state is passed through in lowercase; show it as grey.
  - `overdue`: show the red alert when true.
    - With a recent OCI read: true when the server has an OCI backup policy and there's no confirmed backup in the last 26 hours. Always false when there's no policy.
    - Without OCI data: true when `backup_schedule` is set and the recorded backup time is more than 26 hours old. False when `backup_schedule` is empty.
    - Null when there's neither OCI data nor a recorded backup time.
  - `ssl_expiry`, `ssl_days_left`: SSL certificate expiry date (`YYYY-MM-DD`) and days left (negative once expired). Both null when not entered.
  - `last_restore_test`: date of the last restore test (`YYYY-MM-DD`). Can be null.

  **Errors:** client API errors have an `error_code`. Auth errors come from Frappe and have none.

  - **401** (no error_code): token expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403** (no error_code): no Authorization header sent.
  - **403** `no_client_linked`: the user isn't linked to any client company.

  **Notes:**

  - There is no hosting renewal date. Label the date "SSL certificate expires".
}
